    "Apply a persistent downward bias correction of 2.5 to 4.0 EUR to all forecast horizons, as the model consistently overestimates prices by failing to capture the structural decline from the 76 EUR peak.",
    "Implement a 'lag-to-decline' heuristic: when history shows a sharp drop from a local high (e.g., >75 EUR) followed by sentiment of 0.00 or negative, immediately reduce the forecast slope to match the observed downward trend rather than projecting a flat or rising mean.",
    "Correct for 'overshoot after spikes': if the model forecasts a recovery or stabilization (flat line) after a price drop, force a steeper downward trajectory to align with the actual market behavior of continued erosion.",
    "Treat sentiment values of 0.00 during a downtrend as a signal of 'false neutrality'; do not allow the model to revert to the historical mean (approx. 71 EUR) but instead extend the lower bound (approx. 66-67 EUR) for the full 30-day horizon.",
    "Adjust the 30-day tail forecast to reflect a lower equilibrium floor (64-66 EUR) rather than the model's implied recovery to 72 EUR, as the true outcome demonstrates a sustained lower range."
  ]
